# ── NGS Store backend connection ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to ".env" and paste your Supabase project values.
# Find them in Supabase → Project Settings → API.
#
# Safe to ship in the app (protected by Row-Level Security):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY
#
# NEVER put the "service_role" secret key here or anywhere in the app.
#
# ── Razorpay online payments (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Only the PUBLIC Key ID goes here (safe to ship). The Key Secret + webhook
# secret live in Supabase Edge Function secrets, never in the app.
# Leave blank to keep the simple UPI-QR + Cash-on-delivery flow.
VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# ── TURN relay for in-app voice calls (optional but recommended) ────────────
# STUN (free, built in) connects most calls; TURN relays the ~10-15% behind
# strict/mobile NATs. Easiest free option — Metered Open Relay (20 GB/mo free):
#   1. Sign up at https://dashboard.metered.ca (free)
#   2. Create an app → note its subdomain (e.g. "ngsstore" in ngsstore.metered.live)
#   3. Copy the API key from the dashboard
#   4. Lock the key to your domain (ngsstore.in) in the dashboard to stop abuse
# Then fill these (they ship in the client bundle; the key is meant to be public):
VITE_METERED_APP=
VITE_METERED_KEY=
# — or — static TURN creds from any provider instead of the two above:
# VITE_TURN_URL=turn:host:443?transport=tcp
# VITE_TURN_USER=
# VITE_TURN_CRED=
